## Product vocabulary

- **Headline clash / cluster** — Same story, different framings (cluster or story detail view). Bangla and English outlets stay in that one cluster
- **Story language** — One feed, not a Bangla mode and an English mode. The story title is Bangla when the cluster has a Bangla headline (`deriveTitleBn`; `storySubtitle` hides the Latin cluster title; `buildStoryShareTitle` uses the Bangla title). Each article headline stays as that paper published it. An English-only cluster keeps the English title. Do not translate every article title. Grouping across languages uses a shared place or topic in `story_match.py` (72h), not a translated copy of each headline
- **Perspective** — `neutral` \| `establishment` \| `opposition` \| `international` (`frontend/src/lib/perspectives.ts`). **Political** stories (`topicId` politics) use a government spectrum: for government → against government → neutral → international (`GOVERNMENT_SPECTRUM_ORDER`, `coverageSpectrumModeForStory`). Other topics use **`reporting-spectrum.ts`**: Clickbait → Mixed → Factual → Rumor (`reportingToneForArticle` from rumor flag, sensational headline, then outlet factuality)
- **Bias meter** — Source or cluster lean score
- **Rumor badge** — Low corroboration or speculative coverage (`is_rumor` on articles)
- **Blindspot** — Coverage gap on the **establishment** or **opposition** axis (`lib/blindspot.ts`: **`detectBlindspot`** on enriched article perspectives; **`/blindspot`** feed via **`getBlindspotStories`**; **`BlindspotBanner`** on story detail)
- **Partiality** — One or more perspective buckets still empty while the cluster has ≥2 articles (`lib/partiality.ts`: **`analyzePartiality`**, **`partialityBannerCopy`**); **`PartialityBanner`** on story detail, **`StoryPartialityTeaser`** on feed cards — not the same as blindspot (axis dominance vs missing buckets)
- **Shared ownership** — At least two outlets in a cluster share an owner or parent (`lib/shared-ownership.ts` **`analyzeSharedOwnership`**, using each article’s resolved **`mediaOwnership`**). The story page shows **`SharedOwnershipReveal`** only when **`pickSharpestRevealKind`** picks it (ownership wins a tie with unnamed source). Free readers see the count (`4 outlets, 2 owners`); Pro sees the names. Matrix row **`story_shared_ownership_alerts`** (`PaywallModal` `featureId`). Per-source lines stay free via **`SourceOwnershipLine`**
- **Unnamed source** — Headline or excerpt matches **`সূত্র`** (not সূত্রপাত), **`নাম প্রকাশে অনিচ্ছুক`**, **`সংশ্লিষ্ট`**, or **`sources say`** (`lib/unnamed-source.ts` **`analyzeUnnamedSource`**). **`UnnamedSourceReveal`** appears only when **`pickSharpestRevealKind`** picks it. Free readers see the count (`4 of 6 outlets attribute this to someone they don't name.`); Pro sees which papers hid the name and which outlet printed one. Matrix row **`story_unnamed_source`** (`PaywallModal` `featureId`)
- **Anti-clickbait summary** — **`buildAntiClickbaitBullets`** (RSS-only); **`AntiClickbaitSummaryPanel`** on story detail; **`StoryFeedCard`** bullet list. Matrix row **`anti_clickbait_summary`** — product name “Quick summary from different sources” (UI panel title still mentions anti-clickbait)
- **Story topics** — **`story-topics.ts`** maps cluster **`category`** to home filter chips and card/detail topic labels (BN + EN)
- **Story coverage UI** — header **`StoryCoverageBlock`** (**`CoverageBar`** + compact **`StoryCoverageDetails`**); **`StoryDetailMetaBar`** (published/updated, topic link to home filter); only the sharper of **`SharedOwnershipReveal`** and **`UnnamedSourceReveal`** under the meta bar (**`pickSharpestRevealKind`**); **`StoryTabs`**: default **Coverage** tab (**`StoryArticleFeed`** spectrum filters), **Compare** (**`HeadlineClashTriptych`** + grouped headlines + **`HeadlineCompare`**), **Perspectives** (**`PerspectiveComparison`** with per-bucket headlines)
- **Verified claim** — User-submitted claim with AI verdict + analysis (`verified_claims`, `/verify/[slug]`)
- **khatinews Pro** — Pricing `subscription-plans.ts` (৳15/24h day pass, ৳49/mo, ৳399/yr; **`getYearlyPlanSavings`** in **`PaywallModal`**). Matrix: `subscription-features.ts` — **`PRO_ONLY_FEATURE_IDS`**: **`follow_story`** (home/detail/profile saved stories), **`track_article_clicks`**, **`story_shared_ownership_alerts`** (story-page count for everyone, owner names for Pro via **`SharedOwnershipReveal`**), **`story_unnamed_source`** (story-page count for everyone, which papers hid the name for Pro via **`UnnamedSourceReveal`**), **`custom_topic_radar_alerts`** (profile topic + people follows). **`/pro`** + **`PaywallModal`** (`featureId`). News/browse open to all. **Entitlements**: Supabase `subscriptions` via **`subscription-access.ts`** / **`GET /api/me/pro`**; **`NEXT_PUBLIC_MOCK_PRO`**. PayEurasia checkout planned, not wired.
- **My News Bias (profile)** — Personal left/center/right breakdown from local reading history; optional article-click tracking; media-owner exposure chart; discoverable via **`AuthNav`** → Profile.

## Quality bar

- Match existing naming and file layout; minimal diffs; no drive-by refactors
- Type hints on Python public functions; strict TypeScript on frontend
- Never commit secrets; backend env via `backend/app/core/config.py` and `backend/.env.example`; frontend via `frontend/.env.local` (API URL, optional Supabase keys, optional `NEXT_PUBLIC_MOCK_PRO`)
